# ⭐ What the API image does NOT need — and this file, not the Dockerfile, is where that is enforced.
#
# ⚠️ The measurements that justify each line are in `requirements-api.txt`: the web stack alone is 445 MB
# of wheels the API never imports, and `data/` holds a committed SQLite snapshot the hosted service must
# never read — ⭐ *an image carrying last month's seed is an image that can silently serve it.*

.git/
.github/
venv/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The web app — a different deployment, with a different dependency set.
src/web_streamlit/

# ⚠️⚠️ The committed seed and the local cache. The hosted API reads Postgres; shipping a database file
# would give it something to fall back to **silently** (`config.DB_PATH` falls back to the seed when no
# DSN is set), and a stale board that renders perfectly is the failure ADR-248 exists to make visible.
data/

tests/
spikes/
docs/
mobile/
scripts/
sql/
*.md
